    "## Step 2: Main Simulation Loop\n",
    "\n",
    "Now, we will define the main simulation loop. Each agent will be given a task to perform. The agent will use the `sequential_thinking` tool to plan its approach and the `computer_use` tool to interact with the web UI. We will log the entire process for each agent."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import logging\n",
    "from tinytroupe.utils.logger import setup_agent_logger\n",
    "from gradio_client import Client\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create a directory for logs if it doesn't exist\n",
    "LOGS_DIR = \"logs\"\n",
    "os.makedirs(LOGS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "def run_simulation(agents, website_url, client):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Runs the main simulation loop for a cohort of agents.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    task_description = (f\"Your primary goal is to explore the website at {website_url}. \"\n",
    "                        \"Start by navigating to the homepage. Your task is to find the 'About Us' page and summarize its content. \"\n",
    "                        \"You must use the computer_use tool to simulate clicking on links and navigating the site.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    for agent in agents:\n",
    "        print(f\"\\n--- Starting task for agent: {agent.name} ---\")\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # 1. Set up logging for the agent\n",
    "        log_file = os.path.join(LOGS_DIR, f\"{agent.name}.log\")\n",
    "        setup_agent_logger(agent.name, log_file)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # 2. Define the system prompt with the task and reflection instructions\n",
    "        system_prompt = f\"\"\"\n",
    "        You are {agent.name}, a {agent.get('occupation')}. You have been given the following task:\n",
    "        {task_description}\n",
    "\n",
    "        To accomplish this, you must use a structured thinking process. For each step, you must:\n",
    "        1.  **Plan:** Use the `sequential_thinking` tool to break down the problem and decide on your next concrete action. Focus on what you want to do, not the underlying implementation.\n",
    "        2.  **Act:** Execute the action by calling the `computer_use` tool with the correct action name and parameters. For example, to click on a button with the selector `#about-us`, you would call `computer_use` with the content `'click #about-us'`.\n",
    "        3.  **Reflect:** After each action, use the `THINK` action to reflect on the outcome. Your reflection must cover:\n",
    "            - How you feel about the task or the last action's result.\n",
    "            - What you learned from the result.\n",
    "            - What this means for your overall goal.\n",
    "            - Whether you believe the goal is accomplished.\n",
    "            - Your confidence level in the next step.\n",
    "            - What your next step will be.\n",
    "\n",
    "        When you have found the answer and made your justification, or if you decide you cannot complete the task, your final action must be `DONE`.\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        agent.define(\"system_prompt_override\", system_prompt)\n",
    "\n",
    "        # 3. Run the inner loop until the agent is DONE\n",
    "        computer_tool = next((faculty for faculty in agent._mental_faculties if isinstance(faculty, ComputerUseTool)), None)\n",
    "        actions_list = computer_tool.actions_list if computer_tool else \"No actions found.\"\n",
    "        agent.think(f\"I have received the following task: {task_description} by reflecting on the task and perform the right actions from and {actions_list}\")\n",
    "        agent.act(until_done=True, communication_display=False) # Display is off to keep the notebook clean; see logs instead.\n",
    "        \n",
    "        print(f\"--- Task finished for agent: {agent.name}. See {log_file} for details. ---\")\n",
    "        # Clear the chat for the next agent\n",
    "        client.predict(api_name=\"/clear_chat\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run the simulation\n",
    "run_simulation(agent_cohort, WEBSITE_URL, gradio_client)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Close the persistent driver\n",
    "gradio_client.predict(api_name=\"/close_persistent_driver\")\n"
   ]
  },
